   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## regional-prompting.json\n\nRegional prompting\n\nE15 - regional prompting, core nodes only (no install). Pattern: a GLOBAL style prompt combined with per-region prompts, each wrapped in ConditioningSetAreaPercentage, then ConditioningCombine chains them. RESULT vs a single prompt containing both subjects: the single prompt DROPPED one subject entirely (only the sorceress rendered); regional rendered BOTH in their assigned halves. Objective separation score 9.9 -> 30.0, and the sorceress's blue fell from 9.7% to 0.2% on the left half. CAVEAT: the metric was nearly fooled - the baseline's 'silver on the left' was pale castle masonry, not a knight, so ALWAYS look at the image. For irregular (non-rectangular) regions, swap ConditioningSetAreaPercentage for ConditioningSetMaskAndCombine (also core) with masks from E3/SAM.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S6** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E15** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## regional-prompting.json\n\nRegional prompting\n\nE15 - regional prompting, core nodes only (no install). Pattern: a GLOBAL style prompt combined with per-region prompts, each wrapped in ConditioningSetAreaPercentage, then ConditioningCombine chains them. RESULT vs a single prompt containing both subjects: the single prompt DROPPED one subject entirely (only the sorceress rendered); regional rendered BOTH in their assigned halves. Objective separation score 9.9 -> 30.0, and the sorceress's blue fell from 9.7% to 0.2% on the left half. CAVEAT: the metric was nearly fooled - the baseline's 'silver on the left' was pale castle masonry, not a knight, so ALWAYS look at the image. For irregular (non-rectangular) regions, swap ConditioningSetAreaPercentage for ConditioningSetMaskAndCombine (also core) with masks from E3/SAM.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S6** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E15** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
   "color": "#332922",
   "bgcolor": "#593930"
  }
